{
 "note": [
  "The language pack's vendoring route table: which upstream files, from",
  "which repo at the shared tag, land where in this pack's scaffold — and",
  "how they are adapted on the way in. Hand-maintained.",
  "`node build/vendor.js` executes it and writes test/vendored.json (the",
  "manifest the guard reads); --check verifies without writing.",
  "",
  "THIS ROOT EXISTS BECAUSE THE PACK'S SCAFFOLD IS OUTSIDE SDKGEN'S.",
  "sdkgen's own ts/vendor/routes.json records dart, haskell and lean as",
  "EXCLUDED, saying they need their own route root in this repository. This",
  "is it. Without one, a pack's vendored files are committed content with",
  "nothing verifying they still match upstream — which is what they were",
  "between the pack's creation and this table.",
  "",
  "`version` is HAND-SET per route: the port's own declared version at the",
  "tag where it declares one, the tag string where it declares none.",
  "",
  "`local` UNDER `repo` IS A PER-MACHINE CONVENIENCE, NOT A FACT ABOUT ANY",
  "MACHINE. Those paths are one sibling-checkout layout, kept because",
  "resolving the tag from a checkout already on disk beats cloning; read them",
  "as an EXAMPLE of a layout, never as an assertion that the directory",
  "exists. Anywhere it does not — CI, a container, a different layout — the",
  "runner falls back to a shallow clone into vendor/.cache and vendors",
  "identically, because content is always read with `git show <tag>:<path>`",
  "rather than from a working tree. So the choice of git database cannot",
  "change what lands, and no route here depends on your filesystem.",
  "",
  "haskell's omni port is what makes the target FULL tier: driving the",
  "shared corpus needs the shared runner, and every FULL target has it.",
  "",
  "dart's plugin and sekreto ports arrived with secrets tranche B, which",
  "landed in sdkgen AFTER this pack forked and was stranded by the",
  "migration: the trees were removed from sdkgen (correctly — dart lives",
  "here) and never added here. Recovered at the same tag, through this",
  "table rather than by hand.",
  "",
  "The struct ports had no route at all: committed copies, older than any",
  "tag here, while the corpus a project runs moved with sdkgen's checkpoint.",
  "Routed when this table moved to sdk-20261125-1959-0, the checkpoint",
  "sdkgen vendors its own twenty targets at. lean's plugin and sekreto ports",
  "had no route either, though they carry the header sdkgen's own table",
  "stamped at sdk-20260908-1556-0 before lean left it; routed at the same",
  "checkpoint."
 ],
